1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:06,555
In South Florida, in the dark, a five-foot man is moving a stone heavier than a truck.

2
00:00:06,555 --> 00:00:07,930
Nobody is watching.

3
00:00:07,930 --> 00:00:09,232
That's the legend.

4
00:00:09,232 --> 00:00:15,599
Eleven hundred tons of rock, raised by one man, alone, at night, for twenty-eight years.

5
00:00:16,066 --> 00:00:21,718
Some say he levitated the stones, or sang to them, or bent the earth's magnetism.

6
00:00:21,718 --> 00:00:24,579
Some say he had help from somewhere else.

7
00:00:24,579 --> 00:00:25,556
His only hint?

8
00:00:25,556 --> 00:00:28,766
I have discovered the secrets of the pyramids.

9
00:00:29,233 --> 00:00:31,898
The story always ends the same way.

10
00:00:31,898 --> 00:00:32,888
No witnesses.

11
00:00:32,888 --> 00:00:34,716
So tonight, we fix that.

12
00:00:34,716 --> 00:00:39,133
We stake out the yard, hour by hour, from dusk until dawn.

13
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:41,783
The subject, the yard, the claims.

14
00:00:41,783 --> 00:00:45,381
Then the quarry, the lift, the move and the famous gate.

15
00:00:45,381 --> 00:00:48,399
And at sunrise, we check who else was watching.

16
00:00:48,866 --> 00:00:50,597
Every claim gets a score.

17
00:00:50,597 --> 00:00:52,120
At the end, a verdict.

18
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:53,435
Mystery, or method.

19
00:00:53,435 --> 00:00:54,266
Let's begin.

20
00:00:58,733 --> 00:00:59,858
Log entry one.

21
00:00:59,858 --> 00:01:00,661
Seven p m.

22
00:01:00,661 --> 00:01:01,625
The subject.

23
00:01:01,625 --> 00:01:06,446
Edward Leedskalnin, born in eighteen eighty-seven in Latvia.

24
00:01:06,446 --> 00:01:11,266
About five feet tall and a hundred pounds, in most tellings.

25
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:20,722
The legend says that at twenty-six he was engaged to a girl of sixteen, Agnes Skuvst, who called it off the day before the wedding.

26
00:01:20,722 --> 00:01:26,966
A Latvian researcher later reported that the girl was real, but her name was Hermine Lusis.

27
00:01:27,433 --> 00:01:35,448
Ship records show him sailing from Hamburg in March nineteen twelve, in steerage, and landing in New York in April.

28
00:01:35,448 --> 00:01:41,233
Then a decade of heavy work: Canada, Idaho, the Oregon logging boom, a lumber mill.

29
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:43,071
Remember those jobs.

30
00:01:43,071 --> 00:01:51,163
He came from a family of stonemasons, and spent years in timber country, where one log can outweigh his biggest stone.

31
00:01:51,163 --> 00:01:52,740
That's not a frail man.

32
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:54,866
That's a man who knows rigging.

33
00:01:55,333 --> 00:01:59,430
Believing he had tuberculosis, he moved to South Florida.

34
00:01:59,430 --> 00:02:03,311
A local couple, Ruben Moser and his wife, took him in.

35
00:02:03,311 --> 00:02:09,133
In February nineteen twenty-three, they sold him an acre of land for ten dollars.

36
00:02:09,599 --> 00:02:13,363
And under that acre lay the perfect raw material.

37
00:02:13,363 --> 00:02:15,513
Not coral, despite the name.

38
00:02:15,513 --> 00:02:16,051
Oolite.

39
00:02:16,051 --> 00:02:22,733
A soft, porous limestone of tiny round grains and shell, just inches under the topsoil.

40
00:02:23,199 --> 00:02:28,618
So our subject is a trained mason and a seasoned logger, standing on a free quarry.

41
00:02:28,618 --> 00:02:31,033
Now, let's see what he built with it.

42
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:32,263
Entry two.

43
00:02:32,263 --> 00:02:33,255
Eight thirty.

44
00:02:33,255 --> 00:02:33,942
The yard.

45
00:02:33,942 --> 00:02:38,597
Today it's called Coral Castle, in Homestead, south of Miami.

46
00:02:38,597 --> 00:02:40,352
Ed called it Rock Gate.

47
00:02:40,352 --> 00:02:43,100
Around eleven hundred tons of stone.

48
00:02:43,566 --> 00:02:46,338
An eight-foot wall of upright blocks.

49
00:02:46,338 --> 00:02:50,384
A two-storey tower where he lived, above his workshop.

50
00:02:50,384 --> 00:02:51,583
A crescent moon.

51
00:02:51,583 --> 00:02:52,183
Planets.

52
00:02:52,183 --> 00:02:52,932
A sundial.

53
00:02:52,932 --> 00:02:59,450
A heart-shaped table, a table shaped like Florida, rocking chairs, a bathtub, a throne.

54
00:02:59,450 --> 00:03:00,200
All stone.

55
00:03:00,666 --> 00:03:04,300
The signs boast blocks of fifteen tons on average.

56
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:06,916
Two monoliths twenty-five feet tall.

57
00:03:06,916 --> 00:03:10,042
A thirty-ton block crowning the north wall.

58
00:03:10,042 --> 00:03:11,059
And no mortar.

59
00:03:11,059 --> 00:03:13,966
The stones are held by their own weight.

60
00:03:14,433 --> 00:03:16,668
Hold on to those figures, though.

61
00:03:16,668 --> 00:03:25,066
Sources don't always agree, and one investigator who visited warned that some weights on the signs are probably exaggerated.

62
00:03:25,533 --> 00:03:27,910
Then there's the star of the show.

63
00:03:27,910 --> 00:03:35,530
A gate cut from one slab of stone, said to weigh nine tons, that swung open with the push of a single finger.

64
00:03:35,530 --> 00:03:38,466
By nineteen eighty, it was a TV sensation.

65
00:03:38,933 --> 00:03:41,077
And Ed was not hiding any of it.

66
00:03:41,077 --> 00:03:46,906
He charged ten cents a visit, later twenty-five, and let you in free if you were broke.

67
00:03:46,906 --> 00:03:52,133
Ring the bell twice, and he came down from the tower to give the tour himself.

68
00:03:52,599 --> 00:03:57,126
A public attraction, built by a man who gave the tours himself.

69
00:03:57,126 --> 00:04:01,078
Keep that in mind when you hear the words no witnesses.

70
00:04:01,078 --> 00:04:02,300
Next, the claims.

71
00:04:02,766 --> 00:04:03,626
Entry three.

72
00:04:03,626 --> 00:04:04,199
Ten p m.

73
00:04:04,199 --> 00:04:04,988
The claims.

74
00:04:04,988 --> 00:04:08,141
Asked how he did it, Ed answered in riddles.

75
00:04:08,141 --> 00:04:10,720
It's not difficult, if you know how.

76
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:13,945
I understand the laws of weight and leverage.

77
00:04:13,945 --> 00:04:17,600
And, I have discovered the secrets of the pyramids.

78
00:04:18,066 --> 00:04:20,432
Believers ran with that last line.

79
00:04:20,432 --> 00:04:27,876
If one small man could raise thirty tons alone, maybe he had found the lost method of the ancient builders.

80
00:04:27,876 --> 00:04:30,033
A way to make stone weightless.

81
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:31,695
The legends grew.

82
00:04:31,695 --> 00:04:37,110
Teenagers supposedly spied on him and saw blocks rise like hydrogen balloons.

83
00:04:37,110 --> 00:04:43,300
Others claimed he laid his hands on the stones and sang, like a monk, until they lifted.

84
00:04:43,766 --> 00:04:46,372
The most popular theory is magnetism.

85
00:04:46,372 --> 00:04:54,614
Ed really did write pamphlets about magnetic current, and he described something he called a perpetual motion holder.

86
00:04:54,614 --> 00:04:56,305
To some, that's the key.

87
00:04:56,305 --> 00:04:58,699
He cancelled gravity with magnets.

88
00:04:59,166 --> 00:05:01,679
But they're not engineering manuals.

89
00:05:01,679 --> 00:05:03,494
They're home-made physics.

90
00:05:03,494 --> 00:05:11,033
His perpetual motion holder, one skeptic noted, keeps working only as long as it's plugged into electricity.

91
00:05:11,500 --> 00:05:13,645
The energy theories followed.

92
00:05:13,645 --> 00:05:15,495
Ley lines under the yard.

93
00:05:15,495 --> 00:05:17,641
A grid of harmonic resonance.

94
00:05:17,641 --> 00:05:24,966
Richard Hoagland, of Face on Mars fame, dowsed the site and talked of energy from other dimensions.

95
00:05:25,433 --> 00:05:27,056
And of course, aliens.

96
00:05:27,056 --> 00:05:32,148
Ancient Aliens featured Coral Castle among its mysterious structures.

97
00:05:32,148 --> 00:05:36,871
Books have tied it to Atlantis, the Bermuda Triangle and U F Os.

98
00:05:36,871 --> 00:05:39,233
If he had help, it wasn't human.

99
00:05:39,699 --> 00:05:43,582
That's a lot of power for one quiet man in a flat cap.

100
00:05:43,582 --> 00:05:47,536
So let's stop listening to stories, and watch the work.

101
00:05:47,536 --> 00:05:48,542
Eleven thirty.

102
00:05:48,542 --> 00:05:49,333
The quarry.

103
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:50,591
Entry four.

104
00:05:50,591 --> 00:05:51,598
Eleven thirty.

105
00:05:51,598 --> 00:05:52,390
The quarry.

106
00:05:52,390 --> 00:05:54,764
Ed never needed to haul stone in.

107
00:05:54,764 --> 00:05:58,649
At Rock Gate, he cut it a few feet from his own walls.

108
00:05:58,649 --> 00:06:02,966
The pool and the pit by the north wall are his old quarries.

109
00:06:03,433 --> 00:06:08,946
Oolite is soft enough to cut with hand tools, and it's riddled with holes.

110
00:06:08,946 --> 00:06:14,533
Geologists measure the Miami limestone at around forty percent empty space.

111
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:18,257
He split the blocks from the bedrock with wedges.

112
00:06:18,257 --> 00:06:21,914
The museum says some were old truck springs, sharpened.

113
00:06:21,914 --> 00:06:27,033
He cut channels with saws and chisels, then pried each block free of its bed.

114
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:30,314
His tools survive in the tower workshop.

115
00:06:30,314 --> 00:06:36,648
Chains, hooks, hoists, pulleys, winches, and a wheelbarrow made from a truck's brake drum.

116
00:06:36,648 --> 00:06:38,899
Much of it from scrap car parts.

117
00:06:39,366 --> 00:06:40,563
Now, the weights.

118
00:06:40,563 --> 00:06:43,519
Porous stone is much lighter than granite.

119
00:06:43,519 --> 00:06:48,586
The gate's listed size is eighty-one by ninety-two by twenty-one inches.

120
00:06:48,586 --> 00:06:54,428
With the measured porosity, our math puts it at roughly four to six tons, not nine.

121
00:06:54,428 --> 00:06:59,566
A biologist writing in Skeptic magazine calculated about five and a half.

122
00:07:00,033 --> 00:07:02,061
And yes, he worked at night.

123
00:07:02,061 --> 00:07:05,176
But the reason may be simpler than secrecy.

124
00:07:05,176 --> 00:07:06,770
This is South Florida.

125
00:07:06,770 --> 00:07:09,957
Cutting rock under the midday sun is brutal.

126
00:07:09,957 --> 00:07:13,000
A lantern after dark is just common sense.

127
00:07:13,466 --> 00:07:15,273
So far, nothing strange.

128
00:07:15,273 --> 00:07:19,939
Soft stone, steel wedges, and a man who knows how to use them.

129
00:07:19,939 --> 00:07:22,122
But cutting is the easy part.

130
00:07:22,122 --> 00:07:24,531
Lifting it is the real question.

131
00:07:24,531 --> 00:07:25,133
One a m.

132
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:26,423
Entry five.

133
00:07:26,423 --> 00:07:27,021
One a m.

134
00:07:27,021 --> 00:07:27,695
The lift.

135
00:07:27,695 --> 00:07:30,239
And here, our stakeout gets lucky.

136
00:07:30,239 --> 00:07:32,409
This moment was photographed.

137
00:07:32,409 --> 00:07:36,600
Ed liked to pose with his work for a box Brownie camera.

138
00:07:37,066 --> 00:07:45,739
The pictures show a tall tripod of three poles, like telephone poles, joined at the top, with chains and pulleys hanging from it.

139
00:07:45,739 --> 00:07:48,899
And under it, stone blocks, hanging in the air.

140
00:07:49,366 --> 00:07:53,031
Even the museum's own history now says it plainly.

141
00:07:53,031 --> 00:07:57,576
He used tripod-mounted chain falls and basic block and tackle.

142
00:07:57,576 --> 00:07:59,848
A chain fall is a geared hoist.

143
00:07:59,848 --> 00:08:04,833
Pull a light chain a long way, and the heavy hook rises a short way.

144
00:08:05,300 --> 00:08:07,500
That trade is the whole secret.

145
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:11,687
With enough gearing, one man's pull can raise several tons.

146
00:08:11,687 --> 00:08:16,016
It's slow, metres of chain for every few centimetres of lift.

147
00:08:16,016 --> 00:08:18,288
But slow was never Ed's problem.

148
00:08:18,288 --> 00:08:20,133
He had twenty-eight years.

149
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:26,922
One old objection said that so many pulleys would create too much friction to move anything.

150
00:08:26,922 --> 00:08:32,213
Skeptic Brian Dunning compared that to saying a car can't move in first gear.

151
00:08:32,213 --> 00:08:34,000
Gearing down is the point.

152
00:08:34,466 --> 00:08:39,401
Others say the tripods look too short for the twenty-five-foot monoliths.

153
00:08:39,401 --> 00:08:42,375
But you don't lift a tall stone straight up.

154
00:08:42,375 --> 00:08:46,566
You raise one end, pack it, and walk it upright, step by step.

155
00:08:47,033 --> 00:09:00,047
In Michigan, a retired builder named Wally Wallington showed one man, with only wood, levers and gravity, raising a concrete block of over nineteen thousand pounds and standing it on end.

156
00:09:00,047 --> 00:09:01,299
No pulleys at all.

157
00:09:01,766 --> 00:09:06,295
So the lift has photographs, tools and modern demonstrations.

158
00:09:06,295 --> 00:09:09,339
What it lacks is a single floating stone.

159
00:09:09,339 --> 00:09:10,156
Two thirty.

160
00:09:10,156 --> 00:09:11,566
Time to move house.

161
00:09:12,033 --> 00:09:12,712
Entry six.

162
00:09:12,712 --> 00:09:13,460
Two thirty.

163
00:09:13,460 --> 00:09:14,072
The move.

164
00:09:14,072 --> 00:09:19,509
By the mid thirties, development was creeping toward Ed's Place in Florida City.

165
00:09:19,509 --> 00:09:24,335
In nineteen thirty-four, a gang of young men broke in and attacked him.

166
00:09:24,335 --> 00:09:27,733
He decided to leave, and take his castle with him.

167
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:34,146
In nineteen thirty-six, he bought ten acres about ten miles north, near Homestead.

168
00:09:34,146 --> 00:09:38,933
Then he began moving his multi-ton sculptures, one load at a time.

169
00:09:39,399 --> 00:09:41,731
And here the legend says it again.

170
00:09:41,731 --> 00:09:48,796
People saw the stones travelling up the old Dixie Highway, but no one ever saw him load or unload them.

171
00:09:48,796 --> 00:09:52,500
In some versions, he moved the whole castle overnight.

172
00:09:52,966 --> 00:09:54,011
Ed didn't drive.

173
00:09:54,011 --> 00:10:00,342
So he made a deal with a neighbouring farmer, Bob Biggers, who had a tractor and a heavy trailer.

174
00:10:00,342 --> 00:10:01,713
Ed loaded the stones.

175
00:10:01,713 --> 00:10:02,953
Biggers towed them.

176
00:10:02,953 --> 00:10:06,412
Then, in his sister's sworn account, Ed sent him off.

177
00:10:06,412 --> 00:10:10,133
Go on now, I don't want anyone to bother me while I work.

178
00:10:10,600 --> 00:10:13,864
So the move had a witness, who hauled the cargo.

179
00:10:13,864 --> 00:10:16,244
And he left us a clue about timing.

180
00:10:16,244 --> 00:10:22,433
By Biggers' account, it took Ed three days just to set the obelisk upright at the new site.

181
00:10:22,899 --> 00:10:25,394
The whole move took about three years.

182
00:10:25,394 --> 00:10:27,691
That's not the speed of levitation.

183
00:10:27,691 --> 00:10:33,533
That's the speed of a careful man with chains, a borrowed trailer, and enormous patience.

184
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:38,070
One mystery is left, the one people still travel to touch.

185
00:10:38,070 --> 00:10:38,701
Four a m.

186
00:10:38,701 --> 00:10:39,333
The gate.

187
00:10:39,799 --> 00:10:40,660
Entry seven.

188
00:10:40,660 --> 00:10:41,305
Four a m.

189
00:10:41,305 --> 00:10:42,595
The nine-ton gate.

190
00:10:42,595 --> 00:10:51,987
A slab about seven feet wide, eight feet tall and twenty-one inches thick, fitting its gap in the wall within a quarter of an inch.

191
00:10:51,987 --> 00:10:55,500
For decades, a child could turn it with one hand.

192
00:10:55,966 --> 00:10:56,259
How?

193
00:10:56,259 --> 00:10:59,411
Some said it sat on a natural energy point.

194
00:10:59,411 --> 00:11:04,321
Others, that Ed had found a perfect balance no engineer could copy.

195
00:11:04,321 --> 00:11:07,033
For decades, nobody could see inside.

196
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:10,969
Then, in nineteen eighty-six, it stopped turning.

197
00:11:10,969 --> 00:11:14,721
It took six men and a fifty-ton crane to lift it out.

198
00:11:14,721 --> 00:11:17,200
And inside, they found Ed's secret.

199
00:11:17,666 --> 00:11:27,190
He had drilled a hole straight down through the centre of the slab, slid in a metal shaft, and set the whole thing on an old truck bearing.

200
00:11:27,190 --> 00:11:28,766
The bearing had rusted.

201
00:11:28,766 --> 00:11:29,657
That was all.

202
00:11:29,657 --> 00:11:33,700
One skeptic even reported it as the axle of a Model T Ford.

203
00:11:34,166 --> 00:11:40,721
With a new shaft and bearing, the gate went back on July the twenty-third, nineteen eighty-six.

204
00:11:40,721 --> 00:11:46,378
It failed again in two thousand five and was repaired, but never turned as easily.

205
00:11:46,378 --> 00:11:47,827
Ed had done it alone.

206
00:11:47,827 --> 00:11:49,966
The modern crew needed a crane.

207
00:11:50,433 --> 00:11:56,940
So the greatest mystery of Coral Castle was a well-centred hole and a salvaged bearing.

208
00:11:56,940 --> 00:11:58,062
Brilliant, yes.

209
00:11:58,062 --> 00:11:59,334
Supernatural, no.

210
00:11:59,334 --> 00:12:00,456
Dawn is coming.

211
00:12:00,456 --> 00:12:02,700
Time to ask the last question.

212
00:12:03,166 --> 00:12:04,043
Entry eight.

213
00:12:04,043 --> 00:12:04,921
Five thirty.

214
00:12:04,921 --> 00:12:05,944
The witnesses.

215
00:12:05,944 --> 00:12:10,622
Our stakeout began with the claim that nobody ever saw him work.

216
00:12:10,622 --> 00:12:11,499
So, who did?

217
00:12:11,966 --> 00:12:23,252
His friend Orval Irwin, a building contractor, said he watched Ed quarry stone and raise parts of his wall, and he drew the methods in a book called Mister Can't Is Dead.

218
00:12:23,252 --> 00:12:27,766
He called the mystical theories an insult to his friend's hard work.

219
00:12:28,233 --> 00:12:34,916
Then there are the tripod photographs, and reports of a nineteen forty-four film of him at work.

220
00:12:34,916 --> 00:12:35,821
And visitors.

221
00:12:35,821 --> 00:12:40,137
By nineteen thirty-six, Ed counted more than fifteen thousand.

222
00:12:40,137 --> 00:12:42,156
He wasn't building in secret.

223
00:12:42,156 --> 00:12:43,966
He was running a business.

224
00:12:44,433 --> 00:12:47,175
In late nineteen fifty-one he fell ill.

225
00:12:47,175 --> 00:12:52,588
He hung a sign on the gate, going to the hospital, and took the bus to Miami.

226
00:12:52,588 --> 00:12:54,768
He died there, aged sixty-four.

227
00:12:54,768 --> 00:13:00,533
In his home they found three thousand five hundred dollars, saved from dime tours.

228
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,080
And the aliens?

229
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:08,781
In twenty-eight years of a public, photographed, ticketed project, there is no trace of them.

230
00:13:08,781 --> 00:13:10,222
No strange material.

231
00:13:10,222 --> 00:13:11,663
No unexplained tool.

232
00:13:11,663 --> 00:13:15,266
Only a five-foot mason, his chains, and his stone.

233
00:13:15,733 --> 00:13:16,306
Sunrise.

234
00:13:16,306 --> 00:13:17,812
The stakeout is over.

235
00:13:17,812 --> 00:13:19,533
Time to file the report.

236
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:23,011
One man, building for decades: evidence.

237
00:13:23,011 --> 00:13:26,098
Local porous oolite, not coral: evidence.

238
00:13:26,098 --> 00:13:31,066
Tripods, chain falls and block and tackle, photographed: evidence.

239
00:13:31,066 --> 00:13:35,433
Exactly how he rigged the very biggest blocks: still open.

240
00:13:35,899 --> 00:13:38,521
Nobody ever saw him work: false.

241
00:13:38,521 --> 00:13:42,864
Levitation, magnetism or singing stones: no evidence.

242
00:13:42,864 --> 00:13:46,633
Aliens, or a lost pyramid secret: no evidence.

243
00:13:47,100 --> 00:13:47,941
The verdict.

244
00:13:47,941 --> 00:13:49,344
Method, not mystery.

245
00:13:49,344 --> 00:13:56,848
Coral Castle was built by one stubborn, skilled man with simple machines and almost thirty years of nights.

246
00:13:56,848 --> 00:14:00,494
As one investigator put it, a marvel, not a mystery.

247
00:14:00,494 --> 00:14:03,299
That makes it more impressive, not less.

248
00:14:03,766 --> 00:14:04,500
Next case.

249
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:10,004
A clay disc from Crete, stamped on both sides with symbols nobody can read.

250
00:14:10,004 --> 00:14:12,279
A message, a prayer, or a hoax?

251
00:14:12,279 --> 00:14:13,600
The Phaistos Disc.

252
00:14:14,066 --> 00:14:16,759
Would you have believed the floating stones?

253
00:14:16,759 --> 00:14:21,533
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next case on the stakeout list.
